        <briefdescription>
<para>Inserts the address range. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>If the range overlaps with an existing range, the range that it overlaps with will be returned and the two address ranges will be unioned together in &quot;Ranges&quot;. If a duplicate entry is attempted to be added, the duplicate range will not actually be added and the returned iterator will point to end().</para>
<para>This is used for finding overlapping ranges in the DW_AT_ranges attribute of a <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_d_i_e" kindref="compound">DIE</ref>. It is also used as a set of address ranges that children address ranges must all be contained in. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
